    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a practical, applied view of mathematics—especially in economics and daily life. Though I didn’t pursue it deeply in school, I’ve used it in financial planning and decision-making. My master’s in philosophy helped me appreciate logic and structure, which I see as mathematical in nature. I’m not a mathematician, but I value its role in understanding patterns and systems.",
